  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LAW - access to justice gender based violence in Somalia - LAW - Sexual and Gender based Violence in Somalia</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">LAW - tillg&#xe5;ng till r&#xe4;ttvisa k&#xf6;nsrelaterat v&#xe5;ld Somalia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Den internationella organisationen, Legal Action Worldwide (LAW), har ans&#xf6;kt om finansiering om 9 miljoner kronor f&#xf6;r att genomf&#xf6;ra pilotprojektet &quot;,&quot;Building &quot;legal Agency&quot; for IDPs through increased accountability for human rights violations, with a focus on GBV in Somalia&quot; under perioden 2017-2019. Projektet syftar till att &#xf6;ka ansvarutkr&#xe4;vandet och tillg&#xe5;ngen till r&#xe4;ttvisa f&#xf6;r internflyktingar som blivit utsatta f&#xf6;r v&#xe5;ldsbrott av s&#xe4;kerhetsstyrkor, med fokus p&#xe5; k&#xf6;nsrelaterat v&#xe5;ld, genom att st&#xe4;rka kapacitet hos civilsamh&#xe4;llesorganisationer och r&#xe4;ttsektorn att utreda och &#xe5;tala fall av k&#xf6;nsrelaterat v&#xe5;ld samt inr&#xe4;tta oberoende &#xf6;versynsmyndigheter f&#xf6;r den somaliska polisen i omr&#xe5;den med mycket internflyktingar. Projektet syftar &#xe4;ven till att &#xf6;ka medvetenheten och behovet av &#xe5;tg&#xe4;rder mot k&#xf6;nsrelaterat v&#xe5;ld b&#xe5;de p&#xe5; nationell och internationell niv&#xe5; och p&#xe5; s&#xe5; s&#xe4;tt bidra till en starkare r&#xe4;ttighetskultur inom s&#xe4;kerhetssektorn. Projektet kommer att genomf&#xf6;ras i samarbete med akt&#xf6;rer i civil samh&#xe4;llet, ber&#xf6;rda ministerier och polisen i Mogadishu men med m&#xf6;jlighet till expandering till de s&#xf6;dra och centrala delarna av Somalia under projektperioden. Pilotprojektet kommer genomf&#xf6;ras i n&#xe4;ra samarbetet med UNHCR och andra relevanta akt&#xf6;rer och p&#xe5;g&#xe5;ende program.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The international civil society organisation, Legal Action Worldwide (LAW) has applied to the Embassy for funding of 9 million SEK to carry out the pilot project on &quot;building &quot;legal Agency&quot; for IDPs through increased accountability for human rights violations, with a focus on GBV&quot; in Somalia, during the period 2017-2019. 

The project is focusing on building &quot;legal agency&quot; for IDPs by increasing accountability and access to justice for violations of human rights with a focus on gender based violence (GBV) committed by the security forces.  It will build a skill set amongst IDPs to document and advocate on human rights violations against their community(ies), both at the national and international level. The project will work with Somali actors to create a cadre of human rights enablers within the IDP community itself and those that provide legal representation to them.  An independent Civilian Oversight Board (COB) over the Somali National Police Force will be established in areas containing the highest number of IDPs. The project will be commenced in Mogadishu and expanded in the southern and central regions of Somalia over three years. 

The intervention&#x2019;s total budget is 10 167 500 SEK (1 089 689 USD) , out of which approximately 1 million SEK is supposed to be contributed by another donor (discussions are ongoing with UN WOMEN). Approximately 1 300 000 SEK (142 290 USD) of the intervention budget will be forwarded from LAW to the Somali NGO Witness Somalia for the coordination of the establishment of civilian oversight boards.</narrative>
  </description>
